# TWO nodes a comfortable 0.028 from the upper arc, ONE just 0.01 from the lower. Clearance sends the line ABOVE, past the pair: counting nodes would have sent it within a hair of the single one. Built so the two rules disagree, which the first fixture did not -- there both sides counted zero, and the count rule was never reached
EDIT link_arcs_nearest_not_count ANALYTIC
GRID FREE
DO place 0.2 0.5
EXPECT 1 0 ""
STATE N n0@0.2,0.5 | R  | O n0:0:1 | L n0>n0:1 | D  | C n0 | S n0 | A 1
